From: gts7l project
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qdsp6: q6afe-dai: optional TDM bit clock attribute
 from DT

q6afe_mi2s_set_sysclk() always sets the TDM bit clocks (PRI..QUIN
TDM IBIT/EBIT) to Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_INVERT_COUPLE_NO, so the ADSP
drives them inverted. The Galaxy Tab S7's primary TDM port runs with
clk-attribute 0x0001 (COUPLE_NO, not inverted) on stock, and its CS35L41
amps are set up for that (DSP_A, IB_NF). With the extra inversion the amps
sample on the data transitions. With long sync, slot 0 played clean but
slots 1-3 crackled. With stock's short sync, the amps lost the frames
entirely and their protection DSPs' heartbeat stalled.

Read an optional qcom,tdm-clk-attribute (a Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_*
value) per TDM port node and use it for that port's bit clock. Ports
without the property keep the current inverted default.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 	uint32_t invert_sync;
 	uint32_t data_delay;
 	uint32_t data_align;
+	uint32_t clk_attribute;
 };
 
 struct q6afe_dai_data {
@@ -511,7 +512,9 @@
 					     Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ROOT_DEFAULT,
 					     freq, dir);
 	case Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_PRI_TDM_IBIT ... Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_QUIN_TDM_EBIT:
+		/* Inverted bit clock unless the port's DT node says otherwise */
 		return q6afe_port_set_sysclk(port, clk_id,
+					     dai_data->priv[dai->id].clk_attribute ?:
 					     Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_INVERT_COUPLE_NO,
 					     Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ROOT_DEFAULT,
 					     freq, dir);
@@ -1102,6 +1105,9 @@
 				dev_err(dev, "No Data align from DT\n");
 				break;
 			}
+			/* Optional: Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_* for the bit clock */
+			of_property_read_u32(node, "qcom,tdm-clk-attribute",
+					     &priv->clk_attribute);
 			break;
 		default:
 			break;
